  2026-11-10 - Early desktop prototype implemented and verified locally.
      Action: owner approved Electron for the prototype and requested mesh-only
        desktop transparency. Built the fixture UI with React/TypeScript/Three.js.
      Effect: a native transparent floating mesh, reversible workspace, explicit
        demo routing/confirmation, saved profile selection and honest outcomes.
      Mechanism: narrow sandboxed preload bridge; fixed sphere slots/instancing;
        lazy 3D module; on-demand idle rendering, native/browser hidden pause;
        sequence-bound terminal-state reducer; optional local system speech.
      Evidence: lint/type/build pass, seven unit cases and four actual Electron
        scenarios pass. Native captures verify transparent corner pixels and
        visible graph pixels; full/floating images visually inspected.
      Corrections: first Electron download exceeded the first test timeout;
        the installed binary then launched. Replaced nonexistent transparency
        getter assertions with native pixel capture. Added renderer shortcut
        fallback for injected keyboard events and native minimized-state
        propagation because browser document.hidden did not change in that test.
      Limit: no microphone/wake/ASR/live mesh/Agency/durable jobs or human audio
        acceptance. Three.js lazy chunk warning and development minimatch
        advisory remain documented; production audit was rate-limited.
        Prototype source/build are local, not pushed or released.
      Next: reconcile the same workstream issues/Project identities, persist
        owned continuity and refresh Context Mesh; real integration needs proof.
