  2026-11-11 - Microphone picker and Windows portable candidate verified.
      Action: owner explicitly requested a published prototype EXE and input-device
        choice. Added saved selection, explicit brief audio-only checks, exact
        device constraints, hotplug handling and visible access/storage errors.
      Mechanism: own-frame host permission checks deny camera/other permissions;
        every acquired stream stops in finally. No startup listening, recorder,
        ASR, provider, physical-mic automation or session dispatch was added.
      Evidence: lint/type/build and seven unit cases pass; all six native
        scenarios pass against the packaged executable. The portable launcher
        independently opens its ASAR UI and passes microphone/floating checks
        with a disposable profile and fake media devices, then exits.
        Inspected ASAR has seven runtime files; React/React DOM/Scheduler/Three
        and Electron/Chromium notices included. Private stores, profiles,
        credentials, test artifacts and node_modules are not in the archive.
      Artifact: unsigned Windows x64 portable EXE, 110374894 bytes, SHA-256
        29b7282e592331dfb849143be9e2b9e5a1c4799d7b6415c8aa39607b046953f0.
      Corrections: awaited device loading before hotplug injection and scoped
        microphone status locators to avoid the independent mesh-loading status.
        Fixed a PowerShell command separator before packaged verification.
      Limit: default Electron icon, first-run extraction, no measured startup/
        resource budgets, physical-device/voice acceptance, installer or signing.
        Prerelease upload and remote asset verification are pending.
      Next: commit/push this verified candidate, publish the requested prerelease,
